                "word": "rooted",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "fe02dcaf-4d1d-4c31-923d-9ede3157d3bd",
                        "entry_id": "52bff8a2-a3c1-37d9-adaa-96ecb25a7547",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more rooted"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "b455e306-3390-4e2e-a08e-431a6a093838",
                        "entry_id": "52bff8a2-a3c1-37d9-adaa-96ecb25a7547",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most rooted"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2529fe3e-683c-3f88-984f-f3078019920a",
                        "entry_id": "52bff8a2-a3c1-37d9-adaa-96ecb25a7547",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having roots, or a certain type of roots."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4b92f78e-1ba3-4fb7-a118-960662293bbe",
                                "sense_id": "2529fe3e-683c-3f88-984f-f3078019920a",
                                "text": "deep-rooted"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1c611036-6f02-306d-86e6-513bd565f696",
                        "entry_id": "52bff8a2-a3c1-37d9-adaa-96ecb25a7547",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Fixed in one position; immobile; unable to move."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c6a93782-5d9c-4f75-8efe-e5b118c0e6c1",
                                "sense_id": "1c611036-6f02-306d-86e6-513bd565f696",
                                "text": "She stayed rooted in place."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a2fd5fa9-be8a-4bb0-a40a-b2510bd53a38",
                                "sense_id": "1c611036-6f02-306d-86e6-513bd565f696",
                                "text": "Those with fewest attachments or obligations may be most vulnerable to transitions from a more rooted life, before flight, to the new as-yet unrooted or uprooted life."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb8ecbb0-300f-43b3-ad61-6263f0dee949",
                                "sense_id": "1c611036-6f02-306d-86e6-513bd565f696",
                                "text": "Six successive defeats had left them rooted to the bottom of the Premier League table but, clearly under instructions to attack from the outset, Bolton started far the brighter."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "83c0d7eb-b69f-4cd6-99c3-32a99b0ae49d",
                                "sense_id": "1c611036-6f02-306d-86e6-513bd565f696",
                                "text": "Luján, or, rather, the biped which used to be Luján, walks right up to him. He is a little shorter than Wheeler, but much heavier-set. Rooted to the spot, not thinking clearly, Wheeler holds his violin up, as if this will shield him. The conductor takes the instrument from his unresisting hands and breaks its neck underfoot, perfunctorily, as if crushing a box for recycling."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "14ea7a97-e14c-3896-89b7-eee79f5782c4",
                        "entry_id": "52bff8a2-a3c1-37d9-adaa-96ecb25a7547",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Ingrained, as through repeated use; entrenched; habitual or instinctive."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "90e401b7-9870-455a-8e56-d7a5ce94c0a3",
                                "sense_id": "14ea7a97-e14c-3896-89b7-eee79f5782c4",
                                "text": "1782 May, Isaac Kimber, Edward Kimber (editors), The Link-Boy, The London Magazine, or, Gentleman′s Monthly Intelligencer, Volume 51, page 205,\nHe will immediately break in on their moſt rooted prejudices ; and with a kind of malignant ſatisfaction hack their darling notions with unſparing rigour and unbluſhing inſolence."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "989df755-4936-4da4-8e22-d6ff7145f870",
                                "sense_id": "14ea7a97-e14c-3896-89b7-eee79f5782c4",
                                "text": "The greater part of his property he has acquired himself during years of industry ; but with it he has acquired the most rooted habits of suspicion."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "467b4c5b-81d1-4290-95d2-177812ed583c",
                                "sense_id": "14ea7a97-e14c-3896-89b7-eee79f5782c4",
                                "text": "With other experiences added on top, the feeling state becomes more entrenched, more rooted."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c2eea3ae-3b2d-388e-b419-48739cef9bf6",
                        "entry_id": "52bff8a2-a3c1-37d9-adaa-96ecb25a7547",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having a basic or fundamental connection (to a thing); based, originating (from)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "59848b26-57e6-495b-9c11-2d979d0bb980",
                                "sense_id": "c2eea3ae-3b2d-388e-b419-48739cef9bf6",
                                "text": "Proper Philadelphians, especially before they became Episcopalians, and the unfashionable branches of their families to this day are surely more rooted in Westtown than St. Paul′s, the fashionable favorite."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8e4390e4-9791-47b4-9d60-ab32318e817c",
                                "sense_id": "c2eea3ae-3b2d-388e-b419-48739cef9bf6",
                                "text": "For what is gradually taking hold, I think, is a way of drawing near to God that is far more rooted in history and far more rooted in the gospel than we have been accustomed to."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4d35203f-a2f4-48d9-9719-fdbdebf67baa",
                                "sense_id": "c2eea3ae-3b2d-388e-b419-48739cef9bf6",
                                "text": "This form of humanism posed a greater danger to the monks and clerics than Italian humanism because it was less extravagant, less pagan, and more rooted in an ideal of Christian charity that the church at least nominally shared."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c150cb80-803a-3819-aa60-43c9cccc8e7c",
                        "entry_id": "52bff8a2-a3c1-37d9-adaa-96ecb25a7547",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having a root."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "of a tree or graph"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8b89efe3-c04f-3a00-80d5-f294968863d8",
                        "entry_id": "52bff8a2-a3c1-37d9-adaa-96ecb25a7547",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In trouble or in strife, screwed."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fa0c6821-68bb-41ce-af67-03d854ff41d2",
                                "sense_id": "8b89efe3-c04f-3a00-80d5-f294968863d8",
                                "text": "I am absolutely rooted if Ferris finds out about this"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cbd999e9-1522-3fb7-98fa-c7ae8b67a783",
                        "entry_id": "52bff8a2-a3c1-37d9-adaa-96ecb25a7547",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Broken, damaged, non-functional."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Australia",
                            "New-Zealand",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0d3ded06-dd7a-46d9-89ac-bb933b9f6e9d",
                                "sense_id": "cbd999e9-1522-3fb7-98fa-c7ae8b67a783",
                                "text": "I'm going to have to call a mechanic, my car's rooted."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a9e69937-d67d-3fa5-87dd-3483696445b8",
                        "entry_id": "52bff8a2-a3c1-37d9-adaa-96ecb25a7547",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Having a root (superuser) account that has been compromised."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c7a9f89e-7dc5-4234-b59f-a095061a96fa",
                                "sense_id": "a9e69937-d67d-3fa5-87dd-3483696445b8",
                                "text": "You are rooted. All your base are belong to us."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
